    "created_at": "2016-05-16T14:43:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-16T14:43:15Z",
    "body": "I have no strong preference here but am willing in principle to write patches for the v.nu HTML parser to line it up with whatever we can agree on.\n\n> In https://checker.html5.org/ it reports an error for these cases. It does not report an error for really long entities (like 1000 chars).\n\nhttps://checker.html5.org/ is currently running from an off-master branch of the v.nu HTML parser that has a patch I wrote to align it as well as I could with the current HTML parsing algorithm requirements for dealing with ampersands and character references. There are some parts of the code that I found it pretty difficult to align fully to the spec without getting more review. But I wasn’t able to get the patch reviewed more thoroughly, so ended up landing it on a branch and building v.nu from that.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
